# Glen Elendra's Answer can't be countered, so another Answer is not countered by it (CR 701.6a) and makes no Faerie: Bot2
# casts Lightning Bolt at Bot1 and, over it, its own Answer; Bot1 responds with its Answer. Bot1's resolves first, counters
# the Bolt (one Faerie, not two) and leaves Bot2's Answer on the stack, which then resolves and counters nothing of Bot1's
# (Bot1's Answer is no longer on the stack).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Glen Elendra's Answer
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Lightning Bolt
Glen Elendra's Answer
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Glen Elendra's Answer.Cast
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Glen Elendra's Answer.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
? Stack = Glen Elendra's Answer
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot2.Graveyard = Glen Elendra's Answer; Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
Bot1.Graveyard = Glen Elendra's Answer
